{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "otp-service-collection",
    "name": "OTP Service - Stateless TOTP",
    "description": "Truly stateless TOTP-based OTP service. No database, no in-memory storage. Uses HMAC-signed request tokens to carry state and session tokens as proof of validation.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Call `requestOTP` → get `requestToken`\n2. Call `resendOTP` with `requestToken` → get new `requestToken`\n3. Call `validateOTP` with `requestToken` + `otp` → get `sessionToken`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "requestToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "otp",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Heartbeat Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/HbtChk",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "NSDLMA",
                "otp-service",
                "HbtChk"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Check if the service is running. Returns current timestamp, service name, and version."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "OTP Flow",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Request OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "if (jsonData.requestToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('requestToken', jsonData.requestToken);",
                  "    console.log('requestToken saved to collection variable');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "// Extract OTP from displayMessage in dev mode",
                  "if (jsonData.displayMessage && jsonData.displayMessage.includes('is your OTP')) {",
                  "    var otp = jsonData.displayMessage.split(' ')[3];",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('otp', otp);",
                  "    console.log('OTP extracted: ' + otp);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has requestToken', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('requestToken');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Success is true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"user_name\": \"john_doe\",\n    \"mobileNumber\": \"9876543210\",\n    \"email\": \"john_doe@example.com\",\n    \"params\": \"txn123456abcd\",\n    \"bankCode\": \"IDBI\",\n    \"feature\": \"LOGIN\",\n    \"operationPerformed\": \"OTP_VERIFICATION\",\n    \"messageData\": {\n        \"template\": \"otp_sms\"\n    },\n    \"status\": \"SUCCESS\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/request-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "request-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Step 1** — Generate a TOTP-based OTP for the given mobileNumber/email (identityKey) + params combination.\n\nReturns a signed `requestToken` that must be passed to resendOTP / validateOTP.\n\n**Fields:**\n- `mobileNumber`: 10-digit Indian mobile number (optional if email provided)\n- `email`: Email address (optional if mobileNumber provided)\n- `params`: Unique identifier per OTP request (10-150 alphanumeric chars)\n- `bankCode`: Optional — controls OTP validity (IDBI=5min, SBI=3min, default=2min)\n- `status`: Optional status\n- `messageData`: Object passed to notification API (OTP is injected into it)\n\n**In dev mode**, the OTP is shown in the response message."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Resend OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "if (jsonData.requestToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('requestToken', jsonData.requestToken);",
                  "    console.log('New requestToken saved (timer reset)');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "// Extract OTP from displayMessage in dev mode",
                  "if (jsonData.displayMessage && jsonData.displayMessage.includes('is your OTP')) {",
                  "    var otp = jsonData.displayMessage.split(' ')[3];",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('otp', otp);",
                  "    console.log('New OTP extracted: ' + otp);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has new requestToken', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('requestToken');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Success is true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"requestToken\": \"{{requestToken}}\",\n    \"email\": \"john_doe@example.com\",\n    \"status\": \"SUCCESS\",\n    \"messageData\": {\n        \"template\": \"otp_sms\"\n    }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/resend-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "resend-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Step 2 (optional)** — Resend OTP using the `requestToken` from Step 1.\n\nNo need to resend mobileNumber, params, bankCode — they're embedded in the token. You can optionally pass an updated `email` or `status`.\n\nReturns a **new** `requestToken` with a reset validity timer.\n\n**Auto-chained:** If you run Step 1 first, the `requestToken` variable is automatically populated."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Validate OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "if (jsonData.sessionToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionToken', jsonData.sessionToken);",
                  "    console.log('sessionToken saved — proof of validation');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has sessionToken', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('sessionToken');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Success is true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"requestToken\": \"{{requestToken}}\",\n    \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/validate-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "validate-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Step 3** — Validate the OTP against the TOTP secret embedded in the `requestToken`.\n\nOn success, returns a `sessionToken` — HMAC-signed proof of successful validation.\n\n**Auto-chained:** If you run Step 1 (or Step 2) first, both `requestToken` and `otp` are automatically populated.\n\n**Dev bypass:** Use `000000` as OTP in development mode to skip real validation."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Verify Session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Success is true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Session verified details match', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('identityKey');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"sessionToken\": \"{{sessionToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/verify-session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "NSDLMA",
                "otp-service",
                "sms",
                "verify-session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Step 4** — Verify a `sessionToken` issued from validateOTP.\n\nReturns the decoded session payload (identityKey, mobileNumber, email, params, bankCode, and creation timestamp) if the token signature is valid and has not expired."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Run these in order: **Request → (Resend) → Validate**\n\nThe test scripts auto-save `requestToken` and `otp` as collection variables, so each step chains into the next automatically."
    },
    {
      "name": "Edge Cases",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Validate with Dev Bypass (000000)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"requestToken\": \"{{requestToken}}\",\n    \"otp\": \"000000\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/validate-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "validate-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Dev-mode bypass — `000000` is accepted as a valid OTP in development environment."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate with Wrong OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"requestToken\": \"{{requestToken}}\",\n    \"otp\": \"999999\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/validate-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "validate-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Should return 400 — Invalid OTP."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate with Tampered Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"requestToken\": \"tampered_fake_token.invalid_signature\",\n    \"otp\": \"123456\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/validate-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "validate-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Should return 400 — Invalid request token."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Request OTP - No BankCode (2min default)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.requestToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('requestToken', jsonData.requestToken);",
                  "}",
                  "if (jsonData.displayMessage && jsonData.displayMessage.includes('is your OTP')) {",
                  "    var otp = jsonData.displayMessage.split(' ')[3];",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('otp', otp);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"user_name\": \"alice\",\n    \"mobileNumber\": \"8765432109\",\n    \"params\": \"payment12345ab\",\n    \"feature\": \"PAYMENT\",\n    \"operationPerformed\": \"FUND_TRANSFER\",\n    \"messageData\": {\n        \"template\": \"otp_sms\",\n        \"amount\": \"5000\"\n    }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/request-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "request-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Request OTP without bankCode — defaults to 2-minute validity."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Request OTP - Missing Fields",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"mobileNumber\": \"1234\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sms/request-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sms",
                "request-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Should return 400 — validation errors for missing required fields."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Edge case tests — wrong OTP, tampered tokens, missing fields, no bankCode."
    }
  ]
}